<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 30 June, from 763 to 1997.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pomorie" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pomorie.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/763">763 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,263 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constantine V defeats the Bulgarian khan Telets at Anchialus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Byzantine Emperor Constantine V defeated the Bulgarian khan Telets near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomorie">Anchialus</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast, one of the greatest victories of his long campaigns against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. The defeat deepened a crisis in Bulgaria, where rulers were overthrown in quick succession.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-anchialus-763">Battle of Anchialus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-bulgarian-empire">First Bulgarian Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1398">1398 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">628 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zhu Yunwen ascends the Ming throne as the Jianwen Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the death of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Hongwu Emperor</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a>, his grandson Zhu Yunwen ascended the throne as the Jianwen Emperor. Hongwu had named him successor when his father, the heir apparent Zhu Biao, died in 1392.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1422">1422 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">604 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Duchy of Milan defeats the Swiss at Arbedo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The forces of the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> defeated those of the Swiss Confederation, the alliance of Swiss cantons, at the Battle of Arbedo.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1520">1520 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">506 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cortés flees Tenochtitlan on the Noche Triste</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under attack by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a>, Cortés's forces fought their way out of the city along the causeways at night, losing hundreds of Spaniards and many more Tlaxcalan allies. He returned to besiege it in 1521.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexica">Mexica</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1559">1559 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">467 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry II of France is mortally wounded in a joust</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A splinter from the lance of the Count of Montgomery pierced the king's eye at a tournament in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. His death ten days later left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> to weak young sons on the eve of the Wars of Religion.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1905">1905 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Einstein's paper on special relativity reaches the journal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Annalen der Physik received 'On the Electrodynamics of Moving Bodies', which showed that measurements of time and space depend on motion. E = mc² followed in a short sequel that autumn.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1908">1908 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">118 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tunguska explosion flattens Siberian forest</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An asteroid or comet fragment exploded above the Tunguska river, levelling some 2,000 square km of forest. It is the largest impact event in recorded history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1934">1934 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">92 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler purges the SA in the Night of the Long Knives</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">SS squads killed SA chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernst-rohm">Ernst Röhm</a> and other rivals, including the former chancellor Kurt von Schleicher. The army welcomed the purge, and Hitler's grip on power tightened.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1997">1997 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">29 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain hands Hong Kong back to China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At midnight, at a ceremony attended by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a> and President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiang-zemin">Jiang Zemin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> after 156 years of British rule. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a> became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/special-administrative-regions-of-china">Special Administrative Region</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 30 June <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-viii-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-viii-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles VIII of France</span><span class="tp">1470–1498</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-frederick-i-elector-of-saxony"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-frederick-i-elector-of-saxony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Frederick I, Elector of Saxony</span><span class="tp">1503–1554</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/assia-djebar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/assia-djebar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Assia Djebar</span><span class="tp">1936–2015</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/serzh-sargsyan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/serzh-sargsyan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Serzh Sargsyan</span><span class="tp">b. 1954</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 30 June <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-duke-of-guelders"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-ii-duke-of-guelders.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles II, Duke of Guelders</span><span class="tp">1467–1538</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-lhuyd"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-lhuyd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward Lhuyd</span><span class="tp">1660–1709</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-oglethorpe"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-oglethorpe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James Oglethorpe</span><span class="tp">1696–1785</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dadabhai-naoroji"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dadabhai-naoroji.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Dadabhai Naoroji</span><span class="tp">1825–1917</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-vasconcelos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-vasconcelos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Vasconcelos</span><span class="tp">1882–1959</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
